From: ZonicExists <71136987+zonicisalive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:29:44 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 11/38] bitproxy: automatic IPv6 mode; fix cold-start race with
 libbox setup

Automatic IPv6 mode: while the VPN runs, watch the underlying network
(upstream DefaultNetworkListener). With a global IPv6 address and an
IPv6 default route, the TUN gets the server's IPv6 tunnel address and
DNS uses prefer_ipv4; otherwise IPv4-only. Changes are debounced (5 s)
and re-applied at most every 30 s, so flapping networks can't cause a
restart loop.

Cold-start race (upstream): Application runs Libbox.setup() in a
background job, but a system start (Always-on, boot) can create the
command server first. sing-box then fails with 'open cache.db:
read-only file system' or retries past the 10 s foreground deadline and
the process is killed. The service now waits (max 8 s) for setup before
creating the command server. Verified 10/10 cold starts and reboots.

Upstream hooks: 1 line in Application, 3 in BoxService.
